      "id": "WEN-01",
      "chapter": "global",
      "title": "The two same-row energy budgets",
      "anchor": "global-word-row-energy",
      "statement": "Expanding each grouped vector energy as a sum of real inner products over ordered pairs in the same row gives Φ(G) ≤ (A+2ε)Δ and Φ(N) ≤ (ε+ε′)Δ.",
      "hypotheses": "For the chosen different-word terms, absolute summability, a finite auxiliary index, positive Γ₁, orthogonality of distinct rows at fixed index, corank at least one for same-row pairs with nonzero Gram labels, absolute bounds on large and nonscalar rows, and signed bounds on the main and nongeneric rows.",
      "definitions": [
        "A term's row is (Λ,Λ′,i) and its vector has support at (Λ,Λ′).",
        "A generic orbit admits a representative with an admissible witness and the specified equality of saturated lattices at every finite prime.",
        "The pair corank is the natural subtraction k−dim_E Θ for the first projection of the compatible-pair subspace. The scalar predicate preserves the admissible two coefficients for matched lifts.",
        "Δ=dᵤdᵥ/D*, Φ(S)=Γ₁∑ᵢ‖aᵢ‖². One pair sum takes real parts, the other absolute values of the complex inner products."
      ],
